WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.580
- List of a lifetime is personal for you

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:04.140
because as most people know you have been

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:06.352
fighting breast cancer
for a few years now.

00:00:06.352 --> 00:00:08.970
So how did your diagnosis change,

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:10.300
how you thought about the future?

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:11.667
Because I've had a few friends,

00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:14.860
survivors of cancer one, one did not.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:17.140
And it, and it's, it's one of those things

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:19.120
where I feel like it affects
people in different ways.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:21.420
How do you think it impacted you?

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:25.347
- You know what I hear
a lot is people saying,

00:00:25.347 --> 00:00:28.430
God, you know you just,
you know, seize the day

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:30.700
you live for today and
I'm actually the opposite.

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:33.050
I'm very much like a
planner for tomorrow now.

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:35.820
Whereas, I don't think I was before.

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:39.740
Now I'm, now I'm very focused
on like the future and

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:42.610
and doing yes, everything that I can now,

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:45.240
but I don't live as if
like today is my last day

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:46.929
or tomorrow could be my last day.

00:00:46.929 --> 00:00:47.762
- Yeah.

00:00:47.762 --> 00:00:49.260
- I don't go into that
mindset because if I do,

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:52.680
I think that you're almost
sort of giving into it,

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:55.980
whereas I, I kind of go, yeah,
I'm gonna to live forever.

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:57.050
I'm gonna ya know,

00:00:57.050 --> 00:01:00.420
I'm gonna be that person
with stage four cancer

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:02.650
that lives the longest.

00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:04.240
I'm gonna break all the records.

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:05.073
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:01:05.073 --> 00:01:07.830
(audience claps)

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:10.120
- I'll knock with ya, yep, yep, yep, yep.

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:11.883
- I think that I, I,

00:01:11.883 --> 00:01:15.710
ya know it just doesn't stay
in the forefront of my brain.

00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:17.740
Like the, the, the times I think about it

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:19.380
I take meds every single night.

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:22.760
And that's when I, I
have to think about it

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:23.840
because I'm swallowing pills

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:25.370
and I'm not a good pill swallower.

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:26.203
I'm like terrible at it.

00:01:26.203 --> 00:01:27.770
- Me neither, I'm like almost 40 years old

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:29.860
I can't even, it's it I'm like a child.

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:30.693
- Yeah.

00:01:30.693 --> 00:01:31.526
- But that's so that's the only time

00:01:31.526 --> 00:01:32.830
you're really reminded
you tried it before.

00:01:32.830 --> 00:01:34.910
- Yeah, I mean, you know,
I mean, obviously I go in

00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:36.560
and I get my blood work done once a month

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:39.270
and I get pet scans done every six months.

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:42.100
So there's, you know every
six months it's pretty scary

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:45.700
because you're waiting
for the other shoe to drop

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:46.550
and you know.

00:01:46.550 --> 00:01:47.510
- And what's happening.

00:01:47.510 --> 00:01:48.700
- And what's spread and what's going on.

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:51.350
But other than those times,

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:55.026
I just try to act normal
and believe that like

00:01:55.026 --> 00:01:57.750
life is you know, you just move on.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.812
You just stay positive and live life

00:02:00.812 --> 00:02:02.290
like you normally would

00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:04.040
maybe taking care of
yourself a little bit better.

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:04.873
(audience clapping)

00:02:04.873 --> 00:02:06.480
- Yeah, well we could all do that.

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:07.313
- Right.

00:02:07.313 --> 00:02:10.930
- Anyway yeah, how would you
want to change the perception

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:13.530
when people say stage four,
that's the diagnosis like how.

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:14.363
- Yeah.

00:02:14.363 --> 00:02:15.196
- Cause I know a lot of people will go,

00:02:15.196 --> 00:02:16.170
oh my gosh, then it's over.

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:17.260
A lot of people do that.

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:20.310
It's not, I've had friends
survive stage four situation.

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:22.600
So it's, it's not and I love

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:24.070
I've heard about your mentality about this

00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:26.220
about kind of changing
the narrative on that.

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:28.040
And you even saying like,
look I love working.

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:30.280
I love, it's not, I'm
like like here right now

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:32.380
I wanna do stuff, like is that really what

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:33.910
you're trying to push forward?

00:02:33.910 --> 00:02:35.760
- Yes, because people with stage four

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:37.240
get written off immediately.

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:38.080
- Yeah.

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:40.150
- They get written off
by insurance companies.

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:42.160
They get written off by doctors.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:46.207
They get written off by
you know, your, your boss

00:02:46.207 --> 00:02:50.850
and in truth I think when
you have something like this

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:53.930
happen to you, you're you're
probably an even harder worker

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:55.450
than you ever were.

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:59.910
And for me as an actor, I, I
now have such a wealth of, of,

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:04.800
of emotions to like dig in
and tap into for my acting.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:05.750
- Yeah.

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:08.070
- So I think I'm a better
actor than I ever was.

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:12.450
And, and I, and by myself working

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:14.670
yes, it's helping me for sure.

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:17.460
But it's also sort of putting out there

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:19.769
like hey, don't, don't write us off.

00:03:19.769 --> 00:03:20.816
- Yeah

00:03:20.816 --> 00:03:22.966
- We are we're still vibrant,
we're still out there.

00:03:22.966 --> 00:03:24.640
(audience clapping)

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.990
And we want to be a part of the workforce.

00:03:26.990 --> 00:03:27.823
You know, we, we

00:03:27.823 --> 00:03:28.656
- Yeah.

00:03:28.656 --> 00:03:30.350
- We want to continue to
contribute to the world

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:32.890
and earn money and also so
many people with stage four

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:36.270
have families, you know,
like that depend on them and

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:37.500
and you need the paycheck.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:41.050
Like, you know, we're a,
we're a two income household.

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:42.280
My husband works, I work.

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:44.750
But if I don't work, you know, we suffer.

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:46.470
It's the same if he
doesn't work, we suffer.

00:03:46.470 --> 00:03:47.303
- Like.

00:03:47.303 --> 00:03:48.259
- Yeah.

00:03:48.259 --> 00:03:49.240
- So all of a sudden to say, hey you know

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:51.530
this person has stage four
so they can't work anymore.

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:54.240
You're, you're, you're
taking away a livelihood too.

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:56.640
You're taking, you know,
so it's, it's all of it.

00:03:56.640 --> 00:04:00.510
It's, it's, we are stage four people

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:03.110
have a hell of a lot of life in them.

00:04:03.110 --> 00:04:04.875
- Yeah, and, and you've
got to let them live it.

00:04:04.875 --> 00:04:05.989
(audience clapping)

00:04:05.989 --> 00:04:07.350
- Yeah, Amen.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:08.420
Well as many of you know,

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:11.030
October is Breast Cancer Awareness Month.

00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:13.840
Many men and women are
at risk for this disease

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:15.750
and it's important to catch it early.

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:18.600
So everyone, please
remember to get checked.

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:20.506
A big thank you to Shannon
for sharing her life

00:04:20.506 --> 00:04:24.763
and her story with us. (audience clapping)

